# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- Module#descendants, #autoload_relative, method_defined?'s include_all (Ruby 4.1) ---
#
# Issue #1691. Ruby 4.1 adds, on `Module`:
#
#   descendants -> array                                  (class.c)
#   autoload_relative(const, filename) -> nil             (load.c)
#   method_defined?(symbol, inherit=true, include_all = false) -> true or false
#                                                         (vm_method.c, Feature #22297)
#
# No rbs release through 4.2 declares the first two or the third argument,
# so correct 4.1 code reported `call.undefined-method` or
# `call.wrong-arity`. `descendants` answers classes and modules alike,
# hence `Array[Module]`.
#
# TEMPORARY: delete each entry once the rbs release Rigor bundles declares
# it upstream.
#
# Declared unconditionally, not gated on `target_ruby` (ADR-121 § Rejected
# alternatives; false positives outrank). The new methods sit on a module
# `Module` includes so that a later direct declaration overrides them
# instead of raising `DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError` for the whole class
# (see `process.rbs`). The three-argument `method_defined?` is an `| ...`
# continuation of the upstream declaration, which every supported rbs
# release carries. `interned` and `path` are spelled out because rbs 3.0-3.2
# predate both aliases.
module RigorCoreOverlay
  module Ruby41Module
    def descendants: () -> Array[Module]

    def autoload_relative: (Symbol | string const, string | _ToPath filename) -> nil
  end
end

class Module
  include RigorCoreOverlay::Ruby41Module

  def method_defined?: (Symbol | string name, boolish inherit, boolish include_all) -> bool
                     | ...
end
